    <div class="post-container" id="fpc-2269657">
                      
		<div class="post" id="post-2269657">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,2269657)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-2269657">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/patrick-whelan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2113745); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2113745&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609233321" alt="Patrick Whelan" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2113745)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/patrick-whelan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2113745); return false;" >Patrick Whelan</a></span> <span class="odate time_1428944918 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Apr 2015 17:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2269657">
									

<p>Neutral voting, I thought the story was generally engaging and well written, and I'm a sucker for all things CI really, but there are just so many conceptual issues I couldn't get past.</p>
<p>The characterization of 11 as so shaken by the inhumane treatment of the little girl that she set off the events that precipitated the split of the CI from the Foundation is ridiculous, this is an organization which participates in the genocide of criminals, not to mention to secure the little girl 11 orchestrated the murder of dozens of people, many of whom were likely innocents working in the transportation industry. No one in their leadership would have such selective sensitivity to the value of human life.</p>
<p>That dog just won't hunt. Maybe if the existence of D-Classes had been retconned out, and the split didn't involve the wanton murder of dozens of otherwise innocent people I could believe 11 would actually have such a deep moral objection to the concept of containment of humans, but come on, no one that emotionally compromised is finding their way into the highest echelon of power.</p>
<p>And then 12 came along because he is 11's wife, and 7 came along because 11 said he could&#8230; what, still not run tests on humanoids (something the Foundation does do)? So just read their files, interview them? What exactly is she offering him? The chance not to be ridiculed by his colleagues? And that is enough of an incentive (for someone who is casts in his two sentences of characterisation as more Josef Mengele and less Sigmund Freud) to launch a violent power grab against the strongest organization in the world, knowing full well that 11 has humanistic motivations for organizing this coup? and then 4 is just along for the ride&#8230; why?</p>
<p>11 is the only person with characterisation enough to explain their motivations, and that explanation doesn't make sense. I just can't buy into this.</p>

							</div>

								
					
