					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mandosnamo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1771328); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1771328&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609233321" alt="MandosNamo" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1771328)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mandosnamo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1771328); return false;" >MandosNamo</a></span> <span class="odate time_1428973004 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Apr 2015 00:56</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2270075">
									

<p>My question is why aren't they the serpants hand? If I am correct the hand is all about saving anamolous people, which seems to be the new motivation behind this CI. I don't recall the hand and CI ever really working together. I think in the hub contest you had a little of that idea with cactus man but to then make that the focal point of CI does seem a bit off. At this point it seems like the CI, in being reimagined this way, is moving into territories that are already covered. Like I said earlier as well, if they wanted to go into the helpful side of things there is manna for that, and I personally haven't seen a connection with them. I think this story does provide the basis for the CI being distinctly against the foundation though.</p>
<p>Overall, I enjoyed the story. The above statement is just my concern with this interpretation.</p>

							</div>

								
					
